        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "b23d71cb-6cf5-5086-8ea1-54d2a4faa411",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Griffon Bruxellois, Brussels Griffon, Griffon Belge, Petit Brabançon, English Mastiff, Mastiff\n- Places: Brussels, Belgium\n- Concepts: dog breeds, toy dogs, ancestry, physical traits, temperament\n\nFacts:\n- The Griffon Bruxellois, also called the Brussels Griffon, is a toy dog breed named after Brussels, Belgium.\n- The term Griffon Bruxellois may refer to three breeds: Griffon Bruxellois, Griffon Belge, and Petit Brabançon.\n- The English Mastiff, often called simply the Mastiff, is an extremely large dog breed.\n- The English Mastiff may descend from the ancient Alaunt and Pugnaces Britanniae, with significant input from the Alpine Mastiff in the 19th century.\n- The Mastiff is distinguished by enormous size, a massive head, a limited range of colours, and a black mask.\n- The Mastiff is noted for a gentle and loving nature.",
